The IDE's gutter icons and verification hovers now show the results of both members at a range that a refining module shares with its refinement base (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/423). When a refining module checks again the override of a class member it inherits (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/404), that check belongs to a copy of the member, at the member's own position. The base member and its copy shared one node of the verification tree, and each replaced the other's implementations there, so the gutter showed only the results of whichever reported last: a failing override check, or a failing assertion of the base member, could be shown as verified. The node now keeps the implementations of each, and its line status and hover merge them.
